Thanks for the fix.

Patch 1/2: the fdtfile=CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE.dtb -> DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE.dtb
change makes sense and matches the pattern used by other .env files in the
tree (the preprocessor substitutes DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE but leaves the quoted
CONFIG_ variant untouched). Have you confirmed other milkv_duo variants
(non-256m) don't have the same quoting bug in their .env files? It would be
good to check board/sophgo/milkv_duo/milkv_duo.env too.

Patch 2/2: board_get_usable_ram_top() looks correct, using get_mem_top() the
same way the Xilinx boards do to avoid the no-map DRAM reservation. One
question: size is computed as ALIGN(CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_LEN + total_size, SZ_1M)
without considering CONFIG_SYS_BOOTM_LEN/other reservations that
board_get_usable_ram_top() implementations on some other boards also add in -
can you confirm this covers the cv1800b stack/early malloc requirements with
margin, not just malloc_len+total_size?

Have these fixes been tested on actual Milk-V Duo 256M and Milk-V Duo
hardware showing the LMB reservation failure before/after?
